    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0082" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg816"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terres to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States.</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 153.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 102, of the 21st ultimo, relative to the attachment on the second
                    installment of the indemnity awarded to Richard Allen.</p>
                <p>In accordance with your instructions, I have transmitted to the secretary of
                    state for foreign affairs the views of the Department on the subject.</p>
                <p>I, however, beg leave to inform you that on the 15th ultimo an arrangement was
                    made between Messrs. Devot and Allen by which the former agreed to raise the
                    attachment, and that the amount was duly turned over to this legation by the
                    National Bank of Haiti.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Terres.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
